     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"crown:obtain is an OR of h3_1:traverse and h3_0:obtain, so both must be cut. h3_1:traverse is an OR fed by h1_0:access and h1_2:reach, so no single upstream block (other than h3_1 itself) disables it. No single block can disable both h3_1 and h3_0: blocking h1_0 leaves h3_1 reachable via h1_2. Two blocks suffice, for example {h3_1:traverse, h3_0:obtain}, or {h1_0:access, h1_2:reach}, where blocking h1_0 also kills h2_1 and therefore h3_0. Minimum = 2.\"}"
